# ⚙️ Installation & Setup

Follow the steps below to run Cartify locally.

## 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Manish4343/Cartify.git
```

Move into the project directory:

```bash
cd Cartify
```

---

# 🔧 Backend Setup

Navigate to the backend directory:

```bash
cd Backend
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file:

```env
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret

RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_razorpay_key_id
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your_razorpay_key_secret

ADMIN_NAME=Cartify Admin
ADMIN_EMAIL=your_admin_email
ADMIN_PASSWORD=your_admin_password

FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
NODE_ENV=development
```

Replace the placeholder values with your actual credentials.

Start the backend server:

```bash
npm start
```

Or, if the project uses nodemon:

```bash
npm run dev
```

The backend will run on:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

---

# 🎨 Frontend Setup

Open a new terminal and navigate to the frontend directory:

```bash
cd Frontend
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file:

```env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
```

Start the development server:

```bash
npm run dev
```

The frontend will normally run on:

```text
http://localhost:5173
```

---

# 🔑 Environment Variables

Environment variables are required for database connections, authentication, payment integration, and API communication.

### Backend

```env
PORT=
MONGO_URI=
JWT_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
ADMIN_NAME=
ADMIN_EMAIL=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
FRONTEND_URL=
NODE_ENV=
```

### Frontend

```env
VITE_API_URL=
```

### ⚠️ Security Notice

Never upload your actual `.env` files to GitHub.

Add the following to `.gitignore`:

```gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
```

Use `.env.example` to show other developers which environment variables are required without exposing sensitive credentials.

---

# 🔄 Application Flow

The application follows a typical modern full-stack architecture:

```text
                    User
                     │
                     ▼
              React Frontend
                     │
                     │ REST API Requests
                     ▼
              Express Backend
                     │
          ┌──────────┴──────────┐
          │                     │
          ▼                     ▼
      MongoDB               Razorpay
       Database              Payments
```

The frontend communicates with the backend through REST APIs.

The backend handles:

* Authentication
* Products
* Users
* Cart operations
* Orders
* Reviews
* Payments

MongoDB stores application data, while Razorpay handles online payment processing.

---

# 🔐 Authentication Flow

Cartify uses JWT-based authentication.

The basic authentication flow is:

```text
User Registration/Login
          │
          ▼
      Backend API
          │
          ▼
   Validate Credentials
          │
          ▼
      Generate JWT
          │
          ▼
   Send Token to Client
          │
          ▼
Authenticated Requests
```

Protected APIs require a valid authentication token.

---

# 🛒 Shopping Flow

A typical customer journey looks like:

```text
Browse Products
      ↓
View Product
      ↓
Add to Cart
      ↓
Update Cart
      ↓
Checkout
      ↓
Payment
      ↓
Order Created
      ↓
Order History
```

---

# 💳 Payment Flow

Razorpay is used for online payments.

```text
Customer
   ↓
Checkout
   ↓
Create Payment Order
   ↓
Razorpay
   ↓
Complete Payment
   ↓
Verify Payment
   ↓
Update Order
```

---

# 📡 API Architecture

The backend follows a RESTful API architecture.

Typical API categories include:

```text
/api/users
/api/products
/api/orders
/api/reviews
/api/payment
```

The exact available endpoints may vary depending on the implementation.

